{"id": "correct-dwelling", "ids": "⿱穴是", "title": "Correct Dwelling", "pronunciation": "shì", "bopomofo": "ㄕˋ", "meaning": "A dwelling place that aligns with truth and righteousness; a righteous abode.", "formation": "phono-semantic", "definitions": [{"zh": "正當之居所，合於理義之住處", "en": "A proper dwelling place; a residence that accords with righteousness"}, {"zh": "心靈安頓之所，真理棲息之地", "en": "A place where the spirit finds rest; where truth resides"}], "etymology": "In the spaces between what we build and what we believe, there should have been a character for the dwelling that aligns with moral truth. The ancients understood that a home was not merely shelter, but a manifestation of one's values. This character, combining the cave radical with the affirmation of 'is' or 'correct,' would have captured the profound relationship between physical space and spiritual rectitude—a concept too essential to have been left unwritten.", "source": {"work": "《說文》", "gloss": "⿱穴是，正居也。從穴是聲。承紙切。"}, "components": [{"char": "穴", "meaning": "穴"}, {"char": "是", "meaning": "是"}], "examples": [{"text": "君子必擇⿱穴是而居，不處非義之地。", "translation": "The gentleman must choose a righteous dwelling, not residing in places of impropriety.", "style": "classical"}, {"text": "此山中茅屋雖簡，卻是我心靈的⿱穴是。", "translation": "Though this mountain hut is simple, it is the true dwelling of my spirit.", "style": "contemporary"}], "related": [{"char": "宅", "pinyin": "zhái", "gloss": "residence, dwelling"}, {"char": "室", "pinyin": "shì", "gloss": "room, chamber"}, {"char": "居", "pinyin": "jū", "gloss": "to dwell, reside"}], "tags": ["dwelling", "morality", "philosophy", "residence"], "svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\">\n<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif+TC:wght@400;700&display=swap\");</style>\n<g transform=\"translate(72.39,22.52) scale(0.446191,0.282343) translate(-124.00,803.00) scale(1,-1)\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-wi